WEBVTT

1
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:54.000
Nathan B.: Thanks for joining. Two updates before the plan.

2
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:13.000
Daniel K.: Is the billing number in?

3
00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:39.000
Nathan B.: Launch moves to Tuesday 27 October. The billing estimate came in at 6 engineering days.

4
00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:49.000
Emma C.: Six days is less than I feared.

5
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.000
Nathan B.: Anna's team starts on Monday.

6
00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:33.000
Emma C.: Can annual plans make the 27th?

7
00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:55.000
Nathan B.: Not without legal. And the six days only cover monthly billing.

8
00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:24.000
Nathan B.: So we launch on 27 October with monthly plans only. Annual follows once legal signs off the wording.

9
00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.000
Emma C.: Fine by me.

10
00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:44.000
Daniel K.: So no annual toggle on the page for now.

11
00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:12.000
Nathan B.: Daniel, the pricing page.

12
00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:34.000
Daniel K.: I tested two layouts with three clinic owners.

13
00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:57.000
Daniel K.: For the pricing page: per-practitioner first, trial second, that's the order.

14
00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:05.000
Emma C.: I'll help with the trial copy.

15
00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:14.000
Daniel K.: Thanks.

16
00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:43.000
Nathan B.: What did they look at first?

17
00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:04.000
Daniel K.: I watched what they read first on each layout.

18
00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:27.000
Daniel K.: Three of three clinic owners read the price per practitioner first.

19
00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:36.000
Emma C.: Same as Smith told us on the seventh.

20
00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:44.000
Nathan B.: Good, it's consistent.

21
00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:04.000
Daniel K.: Two layouts: a table and a set of cards.

22
00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:17.000
Emma C.: Which one tested better?

23
00:14:28.000 --> 00:14:33.000
Daniel K.: The table. All three owners found the per-practitioner price faster in it.

24
00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:44.000
Nathan B.: Then the table layout wins.

25
00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:50.000
Daniel K.: Table it is.

26
00:14:58.000 --> 00:15:01.000
Emma C.: The cards were prettier, though.

27
00:17:20.000 --> 00:17:24.000
Emma C.: So who decides on annual at launch?

28
00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:47.000
Nathan B.: Legal still hasn't answered.

29
00:18:05.000 --> 00:18:10.000
Nathan B.: I'll make the call on annual once legal answers.

30
00:18:15.000 --> 00:18:17.000
Emma C.: Before the go/no-go?

31
00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:27.000
Nathan B.: Ideally, yes.

32
00:30:40.000 --> 00:30:42.000
Nathan B.: Launch comms next.

33
00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:03.000
Daniel K.: How big is the waitlist now?

34
00:31:20.000 --> 00:31:29.000
Emma C.: 340 clinics are on the self-serve waitlist. I'll have the launch email ready by Friday for review.

35
00:31:32.000 --> 00:31:34.000
Nathan B.: Friday is good.

36
00:31:45.000 --> 00:31:49.000
Daniel K.: Send me the draft when it's ready.

37
00:34:30.000 --> 00:34:33.000
Emma C.: Who calls it on the 26th?

38
00:34:50.000 --> 00:34:52.000
Nathan B.: Let's split it.

39
00:35:10.000 --> 00:35:17.000
Nathan B.: You own launch-day comms, and I own the go/no-go on 26 October.

40
00:35:18.000 --> 00:35:20.000
Emma C.: Works for me.

41
00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:34.000
Daniel K.: And I'm on the page until then.

42
00:35:40.000 --> 00:35:42.000
Nathan B.: Good.

43
00:40:20.000 --> 00:40:23.000
Nathan B.: Anything else before we wrap?

44
00:40:40.000 --> 00:40:42.000
Emma C.: One thing from support.

45
00:41:00.000 --> 00:41:08.000
Emma C.: What happens to clinics mid-trial on the old plan? Billing needs an answer before 26 October.

46
00:41:12.000 --> 00:41:16.000
Nathan B.: Good question. Billing has to answer that one.

47
00:41:25.000 --> 00:41:27.000
Daniel K.: Before the go/no-go, then.
